# FreeLinX/ports - base/bmake : NetBSD bmake (portable NetBSD make tool).
#
# Real upstream source: https://www.crufty.net/ftp/pub/sjg/bmake.tar.gz
# Portable version of NetBSD's make utility by Simon J. Gerraty.
#
# NOTE on the checksum.  The URL is a *rolling* one: there is no
# bmake-<version>.tar.gz on that server, only bmake.tar.gz, which changes
# whenever Simon Gerraty publishes.  So the checksum below is pinned to one
# specific build, 20260912, and it will stop matching the moment he releases
# the next one.
#
# That is the intended failure, not a defect: the sha256 check in
# mk/project-port.mk stops the build rather than silently compiling whatever
# the server happens to be serving, which is the only thing worth having from
# a moving URL.  The port cannot be pinned properly without a versioned
# archive, and the server does not publish one.  When it next fails, the fix
# is to fetch the new tarball, read the version out of bmake/ChangeLog, and
# put that checksum here.
DISTINFO_NAME=bmake
DISTINFO_ARCHIVE=bmake.tar.gz
DISTINFO_URL=https://www.crufty.net/ftp/pub/sjg/bmake.tar.gz
